GAP: The real series here are modelled body-tide / tidal-stress series for real sites and epochs, NOT instrumental strainmeter records, and neither carries ocean loading. A borrowed instrumental record from a published study's own site remains an open gap.

READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING ANY NUMBER ABOVE. The left column is the INSTRUMENT RESPONSE:
deterministic, no random numbers, and it is the finding. The right column is a MONTE
CARLO estimate on the same grid -- instrument response PLUS event-sampling noise --
printed next to the deterministic value and the analytic floor sqrt(pi/N) so the two
contributions can be told apart by inspection. Where the instrument is flat (the
semidiurnal controls), the MC column IS the sampling floor and nothing else: a 0.1-
0.9% reading there is the re-runner's own N, not a bias. They are not the same
quantity and neither substitutes for the other.

